# SRT.Core (Cursor rule template)

This file is an **install template**. Copy it to the consumer project’s `.cursor/rules/` and keep the package-prefixed filename:

`SRT.Core.CURSOR_RULE.mdc`

## Mandatory

Before using or modifying this package, follow:

- `docs/SRT.Core.AI_RULES.md` (canonical)
- `docs/SRT.Core.API_REFERENCE.md`
- `docs/SRT.Core.COOKBOOK.md` for host Program / BasicProjectConfig

## Working rule

Read docs first. Do not invent APIs. If ambiguous, inspect related code and update the docs.

## Hard constraints (summary)

- Thin host `Program.cs`; no host `UseAuthorization` / `MapControllers`
- Local DI in `BasicProjectConfig.SRT_ConfigBuilder` only
- Project-reference every plugin `GetRequestedFeatures()` will request
- Empty `connectionType` is SQL Server, not PostgreSQL
- Store routing: `IsErrorLogSqlStore` / `IsCacheSqlStore` / Postgres siblings — flags alone are not enough
